      "title": "VRT: fix spectral F1/F2 indices",
      "message": "VRT: fix spectral F1/F2 indices\n\nCurrently, the F1 and F2 indices are reported as a single unsigned\n64-bit value. These fields should be split into two signed 32-bit\nvalues.\n\nFor example, if you decode a packet with F1 index set to -640 and F2\nindex set to 639, you currently get:\n\nF1-F2 Indices: 18446741324930482815\n\nInstead, this should be:\n\nF1 index: -640\nF2 index: 639\n\nCloses issue #20143.\n",
      "author_name": "John Moon",
      "author_email": "john.moon@vts-i.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-10-16T11:06:02.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2024-10-17T00:52:08.000+00:00",
